 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# PRQL dialect doesn't handle null equality comparisons correctly\n\nWhen using the PRQL dialect, equality comparisons with `null` values are not being handled correctly. The parser is not converting equality checks with `null` into the appropriate `IS NULL` or `IS NOT NULL` expressions.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\nfrom sqlglot.dialects.prql import PRQL\n\n# This should convert to \"WHERE a IS NULL\"\nquery1 = 'from x filter a == null'\nparsed1 = parse_one(query1, read='prql')\nprint(parsed1.sql())  # Outputs: SELECT * FROM x WHERE a = NULL (incorrect)\n\n# This should convert to \"WHERE NOT b IS NULL\"\nquery2 = 'from x filter null != b'\nparsed2 = parse_one(query2, read='prql')\nprint(parsed2.sql())  # Outputs: SELECT * FROM x WHERE NULL <> b (incorrect)\n\n# This should handle complex expressions with nulls correctly\nquery3 = 'from x filter (a > 1 || null != b || c != null)'\nparsed3 = parse_one(query3, read='prql')\nprint(parsed3.sql())  # Outputs incorrect SQL with = NULL instead of IS NULL\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nAccording to the PRQL spec (https://prql-lang.org/book/reference/spec/null.html), equality comparisons with `null` should be converted to `IS NULL` or `IS NOT NULL` expressions:\n\n- `a == null` should become `a IS NULL`\n- `null != b` should become `NOT b IS NULL`\n- Complex expressions with nulls should handle these conversions correctly\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe parser is treating `null` as a regular value in equality comparisons, which results in incorrect SQL being generated. In SQL, comparing with `NULL` using `=` or `<>` always returns `UNKNOWN`, not `TRUE` or `FALSE`.\n</issue>\n",
